==============
 gxdm-greeter
==============

----------------------------
gxdm display manager greeter
----------------------------

:Date: May 2014
:Version: gxdm @SDDM_VERSION_STRING@
:Manual section: 1
:Manual group: gxdm

SYNOPSIS
========

gxdm-greeter [OPTIONS...]

DESCRIPTION
===========

gxdm is a display and login manager based on Qt technologies.

Using QtQuick and QML, designers are given the ability to
easily create pleasant, modern looking interfaces for gxdm.

gxdm-greeter is an auxiliary process that displays the greeter, a graphical
user interface to perform the authentication and select the session to run.

It is launched by the gxdm daemon, end users are not meant to run it.

OPTIONS
=======

--theme `PATH`
	Specify theme full path.

--socket `NAME`
	Specify the socket used to communicate with gxdm daemon.

--test-mode
	Start greeter in test mode.

--help, -h
	Show help message and exit.

FILES
=====

**@SYSTEM_CONFIG_DIR@**
        System configuration directory

**@CONFIG_DIR@**
        Local configuration directory

**@CONFIG_FILE@**
	Local configuration file for compatibility

**@DATA_INSTALL_DIR@/themes**
	Where gxdm looks for themes

SEE ALSO
========

**gxdm**\(1\), **gxdm.conf**\(5\)

